---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site';
---
<Base title="About">
  <section class="about-intro">
    <div><h2>Power user / ML engineer</h2><p class="lede">I write about ML, open source, the web, and occasionally using too much compute to investigate my own problems.</p></div>
    <aside class="about-profile" aria-label="Author profile">
      <h2>{site.name}</h2>
      <dl>
        <dt>Location</dt><dd>{site.location || 'Add your location'}</dd>
        <dt>Focus</dt><dd>{site.focus}</dd>
        <dt>Links</dt><dd class="profile-links">{site.github ? <a href={site.github}>GitHub</a> : <span>GitHub (add URL)</span>}{site.linkedin ? <a href={site.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a> : <span>LinkedIn (add URL)</span>}{site.email && <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>Email</a>}</dd>
      </dl>
    </aside>
  </section>
  <section class="about-section" aria-labelledby="about-work">
    <h2 class="about-label" id="about-work">Work</h2>
    <div class="about-bio">
      <h3 class="work-title">About Me</h3>
      <p>I like to describe myself as a power user turned ML engineer.</p>
      <p>
        Throughout my career, I've been drawn to technologies and communities I care about. I've often found that being a genuine user of a product helps me develop stronger intuition for the problems I'm solving.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>I was a Tumblr DAU long before I joined the company, where I spent nearly four years working on recommendations, ranking, content understanding, search, and growth.</li>
        <li>As a kid, I’d spend countless hours going down Wikipedia rabbit holes and eventually found myself working as a Research Engineer at the Wikimedia Foundation on <a href="https://meta.wikimedia.org/wiki/Research:Wiki-Reliability:_A_Large_Scale_Dataset_for_Content_Reliability_on_Wikipedia">content reliability</a>.</li>
        <li>I collaborated with the Tor Project on research into internet censorship across Southeast Asia. [<a href="https://ooni.org/post/indonesia-internet-censorship/">1</a>, <a href="https://ooni.org/post/thailand-internet-censorship/">2</a>, <a href="https://ooni.org/post/myanmar-report/">3</a>]</li>
        <li>I’ve been a Redditor since my teens; now I work at Reddit.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Apparently my career strategy is just to get hired by websites I spend too much time on.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="about-section" aria-labelledby="about-career"><h2 class="about-label" id="about-career">Career</h2><div class="career-entries">{site.career.map(entry => <div class="about-career"><span>{entry.period}</span><div><h3>{entry.title}</h3><p>{entry.description}</p></div></div>)}</div></section>
  <section class="about-section" aria-labelledby="about-facts">
    <h2 class="about-label" id="about-facts">Fun Facts</h2>
    <div class="fun-facts">
      <ul>
        <li>I’m a triplet.</li>
        <li>I grew up in Malaysia.</li>
        <li>I taught myself to code at 14. My first (and still preferred) language is Python.</li>
        <li>I briefly attempted a PhD in Neural Machine Translation. The PhD didn’t survive COVID, but at least I got a <a href="https://aclanthology.org/2020.acl-main.530/">publication</a> out of it?</li>
        <li>I’m passionate about ML, open source, and civic hacktivism.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
